    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "In the great stage of American political theater, the long-reigning incumbent suffered a humiliating end to his long reign. Despite substantially outraising his rival, John Cornyn, the established senator, became the first sitting Republican senator from Texas to lose renomination since 1970—a brutal, televised takedown that ended his bid for a fifth term.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Jester",
        "fragments": [
          "result-1",
          "why-1",
          "how-0"
        ],
        "center": "result-1",
